(5297884, 770096, 83313, '<td valign="top">But have you ever made tie tacks and fridge magnets out of old RAM chips? How about <a href="//www.flickr.com/photos/yospiff/537134189/" rel="nofollow" target="_blank">using hard drives and copier drums for planters</a>, or <a href="//www.flickr.com/photos/yospiff/550416811/" rel="nofollow" target="_blank"> a copier charge corona as a business card holder</a>? Aha, I thought so! I have you out-geeked!</td>', 'But have you ever made tie tacks and fridge magnets out of old RAM chips? How about using hard drives and copier drums for planters, or  a copier charge corona as a business card holder? Aha, I thought so! I have you out-geeked!', '2009-03-09 16:46:14.000000', NULL, 1),
(5297893, 769864, 83313, '<td valign="top">I''m not deep enough for this. I''ll have to get someone like <img alt="'' . substr(''//www.dpchallenge.com/images/user_icon/21.gif'', strrpos(''//www.dpchallenge.com/images/user_icon/21.gif'', ''/'') + 1) . ''" border="0" src="//www.dpchallenge.com/images/user_icon/21.gif"/> <a href="//www.dpchallenge.com/profile.php?USER_ID=50695" rel="nofollow" target="_blank">Posthumous</a> to translate this entry for me.<br/> <br/>A file size of only 75k tells me you could have used less compression and possibly gotten a little more clarity into this image. Always adjust JPEG compression so that your file size is as large as possible, but within the challenge limit. (150k for this one)</td>', 'I''m not deep enough for this. I''ll have to get someone like  Posthumous to translate this entry for me. A file size of only 75k tells me you could have used less compression and possibly gotten a little more clarity into this image. Always adjust JPEG compression so that your file size is as large as possible, but within the challenge limit. (150k for this one)', '2009-03-09 16:49:57.000000', NULL, 1),
