(5350519, 769338, 83313, '<td valign="top">I didn''t bother checking back after the challenge to notice this was one of yours. I was pleased to see whose entry I faved during the challenge. Your abstracts are starting to have a lot of play with light, shadows and texture. It''s shame more folks don''t appreciate these things.</td>', 'I didn''t bother checking back after the challenge to notice this was one of yours. I was pleased to see whose entry I faved during the challenge. Your abstracts are starting to have a lot of play with light, shadows and texture. It''s shame more folks don''t appreciate these things.', '2009-03-14 15:39:00.000000', NULL, 0),
(5354798, 770094, 94815, '<td valign="top">Hi Techo congrats on the ribbon. Good setup and technique. But since I don''t like setups much, I only gave it a five and that was for the fine technique. It''s very competitive here; so I don''t expect to ribbon myself especially without trying setups.</td>', 'Hi Techo congrats on the ribbon. Good setup and technique. But since I don''t like setups much, I only gave it a five and that was for the fine technique. It''s very competitive here; so I don''t expect to ribbon myself especially without trying setups.', '2009-03-14 22:11:57.000000', NULL, 0),
(5356807, 770101, 52130, '<td valign="top"><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by quiet_observation:</b></div><hr/><i> magnolia </i></td></tr></table> <br/> <br/>That''s what I though at first too, but I''ve never seen any with color before and they don''t have a scent. BUT after looking online I guess there are quite a variety of magnolia trees and this is apparently a "Susan Magnolia" or "Tulip Tree" :)</td>', 'Originally posted by quiet_observation: magnolia   That''s what I though at first too, but I''ve never seen any with color before and they don''t have a scent. BUT after looking online I guess there are quite a variety of magnolia trees and this is apparently a "Susan Magnolia" or "Tulip Tree" :)', '2009-03-15 00:03:54.000000', NULL, 0),
