(5505964, 769893, 35357, '<td valign="top">I''ve been looking at some Martin Waugh (SP?) shots, Irene, and I think he''d be proud to call this one of his.  It is truly spectacular.  In fact, I like it more than any I saw on his website.  I watched him working on a water drop collaboration on a Discovery Channel show, amazing.  I''m thinking I have to try for myself.  I think you''re the master of water drops, for sure.  Very inspiring.</td>', 'I''ve been looking at some Martin Waugh (SP?) shots, Irene, and I think he''d be proud to call this one of his.  It is truly spectacular.  In fact, I like it more than any I saw on his website.  I watched him working on a water drop collaboration on a Discovery Channel show, amazing.  I''m thinking I have to try for myself.  I think you''re the master of water drops, for sure.  Very inspiring.', '2009-05-30 18:24:53.000000', NULL, 0),
(5522045, 769622, 69325, '<td valign="top"><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by Blackbox:</b></div><hr/><i> <br/>Did anybody read this? ''Description - Your challenge is to portray your essence without including any part of yourself in the image.'' <br/> <br/>My ''essence'' was that I feel lost in the crowd. How hard was that. Some of you got it and thanks for that. In case you don''t know, here is the meaning of the word ''Essence''. <br/> <br/>es·sence n. - The intrinsic or indispensable properties that serve to characterize or identify something.</i></td></tr></table> <br/> <br/><b>wow</b> here is another definition:<br/>bitter:<br/>adjective<br/> 1. having a harsh, disagreeably acrid taste, like that of aspirin, quinine, wormwood, or aloes. <br/>2. producing one of the four basic taste sensations; not sour, sweet, or salt. <br/>3. hard to bear; grievous; distressful: a bitter sorrow.  <br/>4. causing pain; piercing; stinging: a bitter chill.  <br/>5. characterized by intense antagonism or hostility: bitter hatred.  <br/><b>6. hard to admit or accept: a bitter lesson.</b> <br/>7. resentful or cynical: bitter words. <br/> <br/>in photography, just like many things in life, we grow when we accept the criticism along with the praise. It''s not always easy but being able to look at ourselves and our art subjectively goes along way.<br/> <br/></td>', 'Originally posted by Blackbox: Did anybody read this? ''Description - Your challenge is to portray your essence without including any part of yourself in the image.''  My ''essence'' was that I feel lost in the crowd. How hard was that. Some of you got it and thanks for that. In case you don''t know, here is the meaning of the word ''Essence''.  es·sence n. - The intrinsic or indispensable properties that serve to characterize or identify something.  wow here is another definition:bitter:adjective 1. having a harsh, disagreeably acrid taste, like that of aspirin, quinine, wormwood, or aloes. 2. producing one of the four basic taste sensations; not sour, sweet, or salt. 3. hard to bear; grievous; distressful: a bitter sorrow.  4. causing pain; piercing; stinging: a bitter chill.  5. characterized by intense antagonism or hostility: bitter hatred.  6. hard to admit or accept: a bitter lesson. 7. resentful or cynical: bitter words.  in photography, just like many things in life, we grow when we accept the criticism along with the praise. It''s not always easy but being able to look at ourselves and our art subjectively goes along way. ', '2009-06-10 01:52:57.000000', NULL, 0),
